# Normalize line endings for all text files this repo already stores as
# CRLF (confirmed on server.js, public/index.html, public/css/main.css,
# test_suite.js, etc.) — without this, an editor/tool that writes LF for
# only the lines it touches produces a file that's part-CRLF/part-LF,
# which is exactly what caused the 18716-line false-diff incident earlier
# in this project's history (a line-ending mismatch made git see nearly
# every line as changed). `text=auto eol=crlf` makes git normalize any
# text file to CRLF in the working tree regardless of what a tool wrote,
# so a mixed-EOL edit gets silently corrected on the next `git add`
# instead of producing a misleading diff or a repeat incident.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Never touch line endings in files where they're meaningful or where
# platform-specific tooling expects LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
